Z||000000||Coop88||09-21-2000||01:00 AM||||I'm not trying to nit-pick, but I've noticed that as it's getting colder, my fiero wants to stall when trying to drive it cold. It makes no difference how careful I let the clutch out. I have to give it a lot of gas to get it to go when starting out in 1st. After it warms up, it drives fine. Yes, I can just wait for it to warm up, but I just wanna know if this is normal, or if there's something wrong, so I can correct any problem before it starts to get really cold outside. I really don't need any winter surprises.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||09-21-2000||08:48 AM||||Just a few weeks ago we had this same discussion. I thought I was the only one with this problem, but turns out many people here have it. <BR>My only thought it to run a decarbonizing kit through it. Possibly since the ECM is in closed loop, it uses a default map, not taking into account for carbon build-up, etc? <BR>Ed Parks sells a 3 part kit, and everyone I have spoken with about it, says it is the best they have ever bought. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2000||06:50 PM||||Coop,<P>Are you sure your cold start switch is working OK? One of mine (auto) does that if I don't let it run for a few minutes to warm-up. Fast idle is slow and erattic as well.<BR>Check's in the mail with message on back!||||reg||1
